What does `main.js` print?

```js
// m.js
exports = { a: 1 };

// main.js
console.log(require('./m'));
```

What does this CommonJS script print?

```js
const a = require('./m');
const b = require('./m');
delete require.cache[require.resolve('./m')];
const c = require('./m');
console.log(a === b, a === c);
```

What does this print on Node.js 24?

```js
// e.mjs
export default 42;
export const n = 1;

// r.cjs
const m = require('./e.mjs');
console.log(Object.keys(m), m.default);
```

A package declares this. What does `require('pkg')` return on Node 24?

```json
{
  "main": "./lib/main.js",
  "exports": {
    ".": { "default": "./lib/def.js", "require": "./lib/req.js" }
  }
}
```

A package declares this. Which of the three `require` calls succeed?

```json
"exports": {
  "./*": "./src/*.js",
  "./priv/*": null
}
```

```js
require('p5/util');
require('p5/priv/secret');
require('p5');
```

What does `b.js` log, first while `a.js` is still loading and later from `setImmediate`?

```js
// a.js (entry)
exports.early = 1;
const b = require('./b');
module.exports = { late: 2 };

// b.js
const a = require('./a');
console.log('now', JSON.stringify(a));
setImmediate(() => console.log('later', JSON.stringify(a)));
```

What does this print?

```js
// x.cjs
console.log(this === module.exports);

// y.mjs
console.log(this);
```

Run as `node x.cjs` and then `node y.mjs`.
